 **Parameters:**
-*   **Viewing Directions:** Typically six orthographic views ($\pm \hat{x}, \pm \hat{y}, \pm \hat{z}$) are sufficient for an approximate set of all potentially visible boundary voxels [S1, unofficial]. Increasing the number of directions improves approximation but increases computation [S1, unofficial].
